  <datafield tag="586" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's book by SCAD Graphic Design student Megan King. Hook was awarded an honorable mention in the 8th Annual Juried Student Artist's Book Competition by Juror Jay Fox.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Hook the Book was based off of the script from the hit 1991 classic Hook by directed by Steven Spielberg which was based off of the novels by J.M. Barrie. Hook the Book was created in the summer of 2013, and edited during the Winter of 2015 quarter by Megan L. King while attending SCAD Atlanta. Two typefaces were used in the creation of this book. Caslon Regular was used for Peter, Moira, Jack, Maggie &amp; Wendy. Avenir was used for all the lost boys, including Tootles &amp; Peter for a short time to show the playful and childlike nature of their characters. Caslon Italic was used for all Pirates except for James “Hook whose lines are in Caslon Semi-Bold Italic. All pirates are in some form of Italic to make use of Caslon’s swashes, since they are such a pirate-y thing. The paper used was Mohawk Via Smooth Bright White 70T." -- Artist's statement.</subfield>
  </datafield>
